member.summary:
Extracts the name and detail from the rich text. The name must be a non-empty single-line string.
The detail is optional. In case we have multiple rich strings, we take the first one as the name
and the second one as the detail. Note that we trim the name and detail to remove leading and
take the first line of the multi-line string.


Example:

@code {
private ContactFormModel _contactForm = new();
private bool _isSubmitting;
}


Rich strings:
"code ", "\s", "private ContactFormModel _contactForm = new();\n private bool _isSubmitting;", "}"

Result:
name = "code", detail = "private ContactFormModel _contactForm = new();"

Hides  to prevent validation rule
for  from being registered,
since  does not have thread-affinity.

